sentences.l:
“O friend, since indeed of these things you reminded me and spoke,
they say that many suitors, for your mother's sake,
in the halls, against your will, contrive evil things;

as Pallas Athena stood by that man openly—
if she should so wish to love you, and care for you in her heart,
then one of those men, surely, would forget his marriage.”

Truly, this too you yourself can imagine, how it would have happened,
if alive he had found Aegisthus in the halls,
the son of Atreus, coming from Troy, fair-haired Menelaus;

These, then, came there, and with difficulty the men
escaped destruction, but the ships, against the rocky reefs,
the waves shattered;
